**Moving Beyond Hardcoded Data:**

Real-world test automation requires data from external sources. TestNG's DataProvider can read from any source, making it incredibly flexible.

**1. Reading from CSV Files**

**CSV File (testdata.csv):**
```csv
username,password,expectedResult,errorMessage
valid@test.com,password123,true,
valid@test.com,wrongpass,false,"Invalid credentials"
nonexistent@test.com,password123,false,"User not found"
,"password123",false,"Username required"
valid@test.com,,false,"Password required"
```

**CSV DataProvider:**
```java
public class CSVDataProvider {

    @DataProvider(name = "csvData")
    public static Iterator<Object[]> getCSVData() throws IOException {
        List<Object[]> testData = new ArrayList<>();

        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(
                new FileReader("src/test/resources/testdata.csv"))) {
            String line;
            br.readLine(); // Skip header

            while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
                String[] values = line.split(",");

                String username = values[0].isEmpty() ? null : values[0];
                String password = values[1].isEmpty() ? null : values[1];
                boolean expected = Boolean.parseBoolean(values[2]);
                String errorMessage = values.length > 3 ? values[3] : null;

                TestData data = new TestData(username, password, expected, errorMessage);
                testData.add(new Object[]{data});
            }
        }

        return testData.iterator();
    }
}
```

**2. Reading from Excel Files (using Apache POI)**

**Maven dependency:**
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.apache.poi</groupId>
    <artifactId>poi-ooxml</artifactId>
    <version>5.2.3</version>
</dependency>
```

**Excel DataProvider:**
```java
public class ExcelDataProvider {

    @DataProvider(name = "excelData")
    public static Iterator<Object[]> getExcelData() throws IOException {
        List<Object[]> testData = new ArrayList<>();

        FileInputStream file = new FileInputStream(
            new File("src/test/resources/testdata.xlsx"));
        XSSFWorkbook workbook = new XSSFWorkbook(file);
        XSSFSheet sheet = workbook.getSheetAt(0);

        Iterator<Row> rowIterator = sheet.iterator();
        rowIterator.next(); // Skip header row

        while (rowIterator.hasNext()) {
            Row row = rowIterator.next();

            String username = getCellValue(row.getCell(0));
            String password = getCellValue(row.getCell(1));
            boolean expected = Boolean.parseBoolean(getCellValue(row.getCell(2)));
            String errorMessage = getCellValue(row.getCell(3));

            TestData data = new TestData(username, password, expected, errorMessage);
            testData.add(new Object[]{data});
        }

        workbook.close();
        file.close();
        return testData.iterator();
    }

    private static String getCellValue(Cell cell) {
        if (cell == null) return "";

        switch (cell.getCellType()) {
            case STRING:
                return cell.getStringCellValue();
            case NUMERIC:
                return String.valueOf((int) cell.getNumericCellValue());
            case BOOLEAN:
                return String.valueOf(cell.getBooleanCellValue());
            default:
                return "";
        }
    }
}
```

