        List<Object[]> data = loadData();

        System.out.println("=== DataProvider Statistics ===");
        System.out.println("Total test cases: " + data.size());

        // Log sample of data
        System.out.println("Sample data (first 3 rows):");
        for (int i = 0; i < Math.min(3, data.size()); i++) {
            System.out.println("  Row " + (i+1) + ": " + Arrays.toString(data.get(i)));
        }

        return data.iterator();
    }
}
```

**5. Maintainability Tips**

**DRY Principle (Don't Repeat Yourself):**

```java
// Create reusable DataProvider methods
public class CommonDataProviders {

    @DataProvider(name = "validUsers")
    public static Object[][] getValidUsers() {
        return new Object[][]{
            {"admin@test.com", "admin123"},
            {"user@test.com", "user123"}
        };
    }

    @DataProvider(name = "invalidUsers")
    public static Object[][] getInvalidUsers() {
        return new Object[][]{
            {"invalid@test.com", "wrong"},
            {"", "pass123"},
            {"user@test.com", ""}
        };
    }
}

// Use them across multiple test classes
public class LoginTest {
    @Test(dataProvider = "validUsers", dataProviderClass = CommonDataProviders.class)
    public void testValidLogin(String user, String pass) { }

    @Test(dataProvider = "invalidUsers", dataProviderClass = CommonDataProviders.class)
    public void testInvalidLogin(String user, String pass) { }
}
```

**Parameterize Everything:**

```java
// Avoid hardcoding paths
public class Config {
    public static final String TEST_DATA_PATH = 
        System.getProperty("test.data.path", "src/test/resources/testdata/");

    public static final String DATA_SOURCE = 
        System.getProperty("data.source", "CSV");
}
```

**6. Data Validation**

**Validate Test Data Before Test Execution:**

```java
public class ValidatingDataProvider {

    @DataProvider(name = "validatedData")
    public static Iterator<Object[]> getValidatedData() throws Exception {
        List<TestData> rawData = loadRawData();
        List<TestData> validData = new ArrayList<>();
        List<TestData> invalidData = new ArrayList<>();

        for (TestData data : rawData) {
            if (validateTestData(data)) {
                validData.add(data);
            } else {
                invalidData.add(data);
                System.err.println("Invalid test data: " + data);
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Valid test cases: " + validData.size());
        System.out.println("Invalid test cases: " + invalidData.size());

        if (invalidData.size() > 0) {
            // Option: Fail fast if any invalid data
            // throw new RuntimeException("Invalid test data found");

            // Option: Continue with warning
            System.err.println("WARNING: Continuing with " + invalidData.size() + 
                " invalid test cases excluded");
        }

        List<Object[]> result = new ArrayList<>();
        for (TestData data : validData) {
            result.add(new Object[]{data});
        }
        return result.iterator();
    }

    private static boolean validateTestData(TestData data) {
        if (data.getUsername() == null) return false;
        if (data.getPassword() == null) return false;
        // Additional validation rules
        return true;
    }
}
```

**7. Test Data Versioning**

